    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_80ef240c",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the man in the image",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the bald Black man wearing sunglasses (VisualMaterial entity 'man') as the implied 'you' in the text 'what if i told you'. The text 'what if i told you you and i should find a bed n get freak nasty' directly addresses the viewer, making the user the target of the proposition. The man's serious, iconic appearance (Laurence Fishburne as Morpheus) is used to create a comedic or shocking contrast with the crude proposition, and the user is positioned as the recipient of this proposition, hence projected onto the man.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
